---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { abs, issueUrl, meta } from "../lib/site";
---
<Base title="LureRadar crawler (bot) information" description="What the LureRadar fetcher does, how it identifies itself, the limits it respects, and how site owners can opt out." og="about">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="For site owners" index="BOT" title="The LureRadar" em="fetcher.">
    <p>You are probably here because you saw this User-Agent in your logs:</p>
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <pre tabindex="0"><code>LureRadar/{meta.version} (+{abs("bot/")})</code></pre>
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p>LureRadar looks at newly registered domains whose names suggest a hyped-launch scam (for example a “GTA 6 PC download” site). For each one it may fetch <strong>one page</strong> to look for lure patterns such as fake download buttons or survey gates.</p>
    <h2>Limits it always respects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>At most one request per host per second, a small global concurrency cap, a 10-second deadline and at most 5 redirects.</li>
      <li>Only text/HTML is read, capped at 1 MB. Files and binaries are never downloaded; JavaScript is never executed; no cookies are kept.</li>
      <li>Only hashes and extracted features are stored, never copies of your pages.</li>
      <li>Private, loopback and cloud-metadata addresses are refused (SSRF protection).</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Opting out</h2>
    <p>If you run a legitimate site and want it excluded, <a href={issueUrl("false-positive-review.yml", "[Opt-out] your-domain")}>open an opt-out / dispute request</a>. Legitimate sites are added to the allowlist, which also removes them from every feed on the next run. No reason is needed.</p>
    <p class="muted">The fetcher never submits forms, never logs in, and never attempts to bypass access controls.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>.narrow { max-width: 900px; } pre { margin-bottom: 8px; } ul { color: var(--text-2); padding-left: 1.2em; } li { margin: 8px 0; } p { color: var(--text-2); }</style>
